<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nantucket</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nantucket is an island about 50 kilometres south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-cod">Cape Cod</a> in Massachusetts, long inhabited by Wampanoag people. English settlers bought land there from 1659, and the island was governed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> until it passed to the Province of Massachusetts Bay in 1692. In the 18th and early 19th centuries its port was the leading centre of American whaling.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nantucket.jpg" alt="Nantucket" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Bobak at English Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nantucket-08-2004.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
